# Tidy Agent: local runtime consumption markers for one-time Holdouts.
# These gate whether a real run is still permitted (checked via .exists()
# by evals/run_holdout_v3_e4.py / run_holdout_v4_e4.py) and are therefore
# environment/runtime state, not repo state. The committed, permanent
# record of a consumption event lives in the sibling, tracked
# consumption_record.json instead -- see the "Holdout protocol" section in
# projects/tidy-agent/README.md.
projects/tidy-agent/evals/holdout_v3/CONSUMED.json
projects/tidy-agent/evals/holdout_v4/CONSUMED.json
